1. Introduction

Software as a Service (SaaS) is a cloud-based software delivery model. It allows users to access applications through the internet without installing software on their computers.

A cloud-based attendance management system helps colleges maintain student attendance digitally. Faculty members can mark attendance and students can check their attendance from anywhere.

2. Problem Analysis

In many colleges, attendance is maintained manually using registers and Excel sheets. This process takes more time and may cause calculation errors, data loss and difficulties in maintaining records.

To solve these problems, a cloud-based attendance management system can be developed using the SaaS model.

3. Proposed Solution

The proposed system uses SaaS technology to store and manage attendance records online.

Faculty members can log in using their accounts and mark student attendance. Students can log in to view their attendance percentage and daily attendance details.

The system stores all information securely in a cloud database.

4. Essential Features

1. Login System: Separate login facilities for faculty and students.
2. Attendance Marking: Faculty can mark students as present or absent.
3. Attendance Reports: Students can view their attendance percentage.
4. Cloud Storage: Attendance records are stored online and can be accessed anytime.

5. Benefits of Cloud-Based Applications

1. Easy Access: Faculty and students can access the system from anywhere using the internet.
2. Time Saving: Digital attendance reduces manual work and saves time.
3. Data Storage: Attendance information is stored online and is easy to manage.

6. Challenges

1. Internet Dependency: The system requires an internet connection to access attendance records.
2. Data Security: Student information must be protected from unauthorized access.

